From b32fcd7d62683993073480e5e1c0aa5ebdbb9811 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: genetixteam <genetixteam@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 16:13:39 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] econet: EX20v v2: bring over the v1 port's runtime tuning

The v1 port ships userspace defaults next to its econet-eth driver that
the v2 image was missing:

- 90-ex20v-wan-ipv6: disable the dynamic wan_6 on the PPPoE WAN; netifd
  otherwise respawns it in a loop that eats a whole CPU.
- packet-steering.sh: keep the ethernet/mt76 NAPI cores free and steer
  NAT/PPPoE forwarding onto CPU1+CPU3 via RPS.
- 05-econet-board-json: regenerate an empty /etc/board.json on first boot.
- 96-ex20v-timezone: Europe/Istanbul, hostname EX20v.
- ex20v-iptv: apply the IPTV VLAN bridge choice through the driver's
  debugfs knob.

Board checks accept both tplink,ex20v and tplink,ex20v-v2.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01YbeF2izcaoFj6qx1YBoB3j
